"""erhai-lab: GPU runtime-PM lab for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai, SM8750).

One stdlib-only tool, forked from erhai-sleep-lab. Subcommands:

  fetch <candidate>   download a CI-built lab kernel, verify SHA256SUMS and the
                      UKI/modules kernelrelease, install it beside the package
                      kernel (/boot/<kver>.efi + /usr/lib/modules/<kver>/)
                      (--from-dir DIR: a local tools/build-local.sh build instead)
  whoami              print the booted kernel's lab candidate, build and stack
  setup               (root) install the g1 tools via the installed setup.sh and
                      build the pinned IGT msm_recovery under /var/lib/erhai-gpu/igt
  mode once|always    (root) set MODE= in /etc/erhai/gpu-pin.conf, enable its pin
                      service and disable the other; takes effect at the next boot
  queue <label> --expect <cand|package>
                      (root) queue a g0 check for the next boot of that kernel
  boot-run            (root, boot service) log this boot, run the queued g0 if the
                      expected kernel booted
  status              whoami, MODE, queue, recent boots and evidence
  g1 [--runs 5] [--hangcheck 1] [--pinned] [--yes]
                      (root) run IGT msm_recovery per the ladder, stop at the first FAIL;
                      this is the only subcommand that hangs the GPU
  power [--minutes N] (root) sample the battery V*I while idle on battery and compare
                      the average with the 3639 mW baseline (default 30 minutes)
  soak start|stop|tick|status
                      g2: count GPU runtime-PM cycles across reboots with an hourly
                      timer; start/stop/tick need root, status shows hours, cycles,
                      boots, resets and GPU wedge lines
  report [--out FILE] all evidence as Markdown for the ladder Results (no root; run as
                      root to include the soak's kernel wedge lines)

Rungs, experiments and their numbers are described in docs/ladder.md.
"""

